  "behavior": [
    "Service emits same-instance failed/cleanupPending=false only before acquiring a terminal adapter; Main preserves current-instance failure proof, ignoring old bindings and retaining unknown without proof.",
    "Failed terminal with unknown cleanup explicitly rejects reconnect; running/starting/closing remain idempotent.",
    "Fixture strictly verifies trusted public key and signature; private keys and auth socket stay temporary and are never archived.",
    "Final owned profiles, keys, server, agent and PTY helpers are cleaned; helper bootstrap removed after app termination.",
    "Expected disconnect leaves product cleanupPending=true; test fixture separately confirms both owned PTYs exited and force-exits only its Electron. This is not normal product shutdown acceptance."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Mac remains locked; no native-focus, real drag or OS IME acceptance. Chinese PTY output is generated by ASCII POSIX octal printf through the actual terminal UI; Playwright direct Chinese typing and old bash Unicode escape failed in early fixtures.",
    "First product failure log preserved but its original context/body-only attachment was not persisted before Playwright cleared outputs. Subsequent available contexts are archived; v3/v4 JSON attachments are explicitly on disk.",
    "Initial service/Main before run had a transient Main proof assertion; corrected before-v2 waits launch completion and records two real failures.",
    "First formal type/lint failures and v2 Playwright collection failure are preserved; v3 full-unit MCP test synchronization failure is preserved. Only v4 receipts are final.",
    "Early fifth run timed out during deliberately refused unknown-cleanup window close and worker teardown; exact owned PID inspection/termination and leftover directory cleanup are in phase4b-ssh-fifth-cleanup.json. No normal shutdown pass is claimed for this path.",
    "External production SSH hosts, packaged Electron and actual real-model observation live are not run in this package."
